# L §5.11 missing(): the outlier example, copied whole (with pnl, var and version mar32).  "missing(r) is true
# when the read r is a hole because no row gives it, or its row is a stated ?, and false otherwise; it is never
# itself a hole. ... Every result that such a rule decides, where a missing test in its when read true and the rule
# won, lists it in its register: missing record counted by <version>."  On 2026-03-02 pnl has no row: true,
# counted by mar32.  On 2026-03-03 pnl = -5, var = 2: base, -5 < -2, true, with no register entry of its own.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
source rule32 "MAR art. 32"

input pnl[d in days]: num
input var[d in days]: num

def outlier[d in days]: bool at d
  rule base = pnl[d] < -var[d]
  rule no_record beats base v mar32 = true when missing(pnl[d]) or missing(var[d])

version mar32
  cite rule32
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01

version data
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pnl[2026-03-03] = -5
  var[2026-03-02] = 2
  var[2026-03-03] = 2

ask q1: outlier[2026-03-02], outlier[2026-03-03]
ask q2: outlier[2026-03-02]
=== expect
q1: (true, true)
  missing record counted by mar32
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: true
  missing record counted by mar32
  cut 2026-12-31
